// test-error
// Issue #1353, cross-file: value-consumer.cnx reads a const declared in
// value-source.cnx without including it.
//
// #1502 review: paired with undeclared-value-sibling-consumer-first.test.cnx
// — same two sources, opposite include order, and the two must produce the
// IDENTICAL diagnostic set. `knownVariables` is assembled from
// `getSymbolInfoByFileMap()`, which Transpiler.ts documents at the call site
// as filled incrementally and order-sensitive, so "stage 5 reads a complete
// map" is a property this pair asserts rather than a comment anyone has to
// trust. #1430 is the same analyzer failing in exactly this way.
//
// Both halves carry the `-first` suffix on purpose: scripts/__tests__/
// order-pair-fixtures.test.ts treats that name as a promise of a pair and
// fails a directory holding a lone half. This fixture was `undeclared-value-
// sibling.test.cnx` until the twin was added.
#include <value-source.cnx>
#include <value-consumer.cnx>

u32 main() {
    return 0;
}
